<title>NORWAY: RGI books 100 mln NOK profit on share sale.</title>
<headline>RGI books 100 mln NOK profit on share sale.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian investment group RGI said on Tuesday it would book a profit of 100 million crowns on the sale of 2.36 million shares in real estate company Avantor ASA earlier in the day.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale was made to create more liquidity in the share,&quot; RGI spokesman Per Eikrem told Reuters. &quot;RGI has no immediate plans to sell more.&quot;</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
